From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 05:39:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: disable CP0 watch probing on SF2000

The SF2000 bring-up kernel does not need hardware watchpoints, and probing
optional CP0 watch registers is another early boot hazard on partially matched
HC15xx/SF2000 emulation. Clear the watch capability before the generic probe
loop so both QEMU and hardware can continue through CPU setup using the
MIPS32r1-first path.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
index 65db45fc5a99..b072a7c2d14e 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -778,6 +778,9 @@ static void decode_configs(struct cpuinfo_mips *c)
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
+		c->options &= ~MIPS_CPU_WATCH;
+
 	/* configure the FTLB write probability */
 	set_ftlb_enable(c, (mips_ftlb_disabled ? 0 : FTLB_EN) | FTLB_SET_PROB);
 
-- 
